    "outcome": "Allowed standing wave patterns in a pipe closed at one end",
    "stem": {
     "type": "doc",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "content": [
        {
         "marks": [],
         "type": "text",
         "text": "A tube of length 0.17 m is closed at one end and open at the other end. The air in the tube vibrates in its first harmonic at a frequency of 500 Hz. The speed of sound in air is 340 m s⁻¹."
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "type": "paragraph",
       "content": [
        {
         "marks": [],
         "type": "text",
         "text": "What is the next higher frequency at which a standing wave can be formed in the tube?"
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    "stimuli": [],
    "mcq": {
     "option_kind": "numeric_with_unit",
     "option_layout": "single_value",
     "column_headers": [],
     "statements": [],
     "options": [
      {
       "key": "A",
       "cells": [
        {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "content": [
            {
             "marks": [],
             "type": "text",
             "text": "1000 Hz"
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ],
       "rationale": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
           {
            "marks": [],
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Assumes that all whole-number multiples of the first harmonic also occur in a pipe closed at one end: 2 × 500 = 1000 Hz (this pattern does not satisfy the node condition at the closed end)"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "key": "B",
       "cells": [
        {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "content": [
            {
             "marks": [],
             "type": "text",
             "text": "1500 Hz"
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ],
       "rationale": null
      },
      {
       "key": "C",
       "cells": [
        {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "content": [
            {
             "marks": [],
             "type": "text",
             "text": "2500 Hz"
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ],
       "rationale": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
           {
            "marks": [],
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Skips an allowed pattern (L = 5λ/4): 5 × 500 = 2500 Hz; a standing wave forms at this frequency but it is not the \"next\" one"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      },
      {
       "key": "D",
       "cells": [
        {
         "type": "doc",
         "content": [
          {
           "type": "paragraph",
           "content": [
            {
             "marks": [],
             "type": "text",
             "text": "3000 Hz"
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ],
       "rationale": {
        "type": "doc",
        "content": [
         {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
           {
            "marks": [],
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Uses the relation for a pipe open at both ends for the third harmonic: 3 × 340 / (2 × 0.17) = 3000 Hz"
           }
          ]
         }
        ]
       }
      }
     ],
     "correct_key": "B",
     "explanation": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
       {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
         {
          "marks": [],
          "type": "text",
          "text": "There is a displacement node at the closed end and an antinode at the open end. First harmonic: L = λ/4 → f₁ = 340 / (4 × 0.17) = 500 Hz. The next allowed pattern: L = 3λ/4 → λ = 0.227 m → f = 3 × 500 = 1500 Hz."
         }
        ]
       }
      ]
     },
